{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really","id":9295,"title":"Attention Deva players! (And other scion players really)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-12T16:44:21-08:00","id":9295,"title":"Attention Deva players! (And other scion players really)","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I somehow convinced my teacher in my college course to let me look at the use of Hinduism in table-top RPGs and video games. He allowed this as long as I could actually talk with players of these games and get their opinion. So I have come here to ask you some simple questions and I would really appreciate it if you could help by answering them.<br /> <br /> The questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?<br /> <br /> 2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?<br /> <br /> 3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1057,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1057-loki-duck","user":"Loki Duck","date":".  Deva, Hinduism 11-12-2013, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1057-loki-duck","name":"Loki Duck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:55:28-08:00","id":9310,"title":"","content":"<i>1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?</i><br /> Based on myth and religions for fun.<br /> I try not to go beyond that.<br /> <br /> <i>2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?</i><br /> Read a lot of books on various religious beliefs. Hinduism was a part of it all.<br /> <br /> <i>3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?</i><br /> *shrugs* Not too sure I feel the need to know more, although I was curious to know if any non-Indian ever converted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:56:03-08:00","id":9313,"title":"","content":"1. In some cases, I feel the writers did it right in some portrayals of the Gods while others were definitely wrong (IE: Pan as Satan, Loki having Fire associated). All in all, I know it was made for fun and that's ok.<br /> <br /> 2. I knew a bit about the Devas from my own interest in mythology on a general level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/601-dioscuri","name":"Dioscuri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:09:43-08:00","id":9324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're.. as accurate as your average pop-culture representation of history and mythology. Scion is working through a modern, Western cultural view of the world and other religions. It's fairly common and obviously causes some issues with realism, but they have a product to sell and deadlines to meet. Their goal is creating a fun game based on mythology and using mythic figures as background for telling modern stories. They do not have the time or resources to write historically and culturally accurate depictions of each religion, much less work out a way to seamlessly integrate dozens of different religions and cultures together. So things are treated very basically, with very little depth and a great deal of artistic license. It's about par for the course, or maybe a bit above par, considering how stuff like Marvel's version of Thor deals with mythology. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've taken some religious studies classes and I love mythology in general. I've read segments of the Vedas and I'm generally familiar with several of the more famous stories and figures in Vedic mythology. Not my favorite mythology (woo! ancient near eastern!) but still very cool stuff. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, yes, but not directly through their presentation of the Hindus. More it was just that playing and running Scion tends to encourage more of an interest in mythology in general, by pushing you to harvest ideas for stories and characters from world religions. I did a lot more reading about some obscure figures like Nirrti because of running Scion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:46:57-08:00","id":9348,"title":"","content":"1. To the best of my knowledge, they're pretty good. I've certainly seen worse. However, I believe that as a Western company trying to write a global set of pantheons for a (mostly) Western audience, White Wolf did a pretty good job given their budget and resource constraints and the necessity of gamifying everything.<br /> <br /> 2. Not that much. I keep meaning to read the Vedas and/or Baghavad Gita and/or Ramayana, but getting sidetracked by books that are less intense undertakings.<br /> <br /> 3. I wanted to already, but just never had the time for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T17:57:52-08:00","id":9356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I somehow convinced my teacher in my college course to let me look at the use of Hinduism in table-top RPGs and video games. He allowed this as long as I could actually talk with players of these games and get their opinion. So I have come here to ask you some simple questions and I would really appreciate it if you could help by answering them.<br /> <br /> The questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?<br /> <br /> 2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?<br /> <br /> 3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. They might not be accurate but they are far superior to other fictional representations.<br /> 2. It's extremely complicated and highly difficult for westerners to understand.<br /> 3. I tried to learn about it before but ran into people who were insufficient teachers. So no. I would rather be shot in the forehead with a rubber bullet then be taught Hinduism again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/952-exdeath","name":"ExDeath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar952_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:40:03-08:00","id":9386,"title":"","content":"1. The pantheons are a nice introduction to mythologies not normally taught in American schools. There are a lot of problems, but even a casual reading introduces a wide range of characters and concepts unfamiliar to the average Joe. <br /> <br /> 2. I studied Hinduism as a possible personal option; I also worked on a focus-project about Hinduism in high school, and tried to read the Ramayana. Once. <br /> <br /> 3. The game definitely made me want to learn more about a wide variety of mythologies, and I've since spent countless hours looking things up on the internet on a purely hobby-level basis. However, I tend to avoid stuff on Hindu mythology because I think I 'know enough', and because I don't like the smell of curry. Stupid reasons I know, but their are such a wide variety of interesting religions to learn about, I've got to pick and choose somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/911-phoebuslore","name":"phoebuslore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar911_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:19:16-08:00","id":9621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?<br /> <br /> 2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?<br /> <br /> 3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I like the game, but they're pretty hit and miss. Given the spread of favoured domains and attributes they obviously weren't optimising for game balance. As far accuracy and sensitivity go I think they did alright, but mythology is such a deep and complex field that it's inevitable that there will be different interpretations for a few of their choices and that some of them will be almost entirely wrong. Even so, I think they did pretty will for your average RPG.<br /> <br /> 2) Bits and pieces from incidental reading, more from random pop culture exposure: the Mahabharata TV series and the absolutely stunning Lords of Light novel by Roger Zelazny.<br /> <br /> 3) If I were currently playing I would definitely read up on the more and be interested in using them in the game. As a gamer I tend to get a little intrigued by real world mythology whenever I come across it, and this certainly piqued my interest for Hindu-wise*<br /> <br /> *no offence to people who follow it as a religion, but its the mythological aspects of it that interest me, not the theological ones, if that makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/630-vidiian","name":"Vidiian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T06:47:24-08:00","id":12036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavily fictionalized and not very well connected to actual mythologies. Some of this seems intentional (what are gods doing in the world nowadays?) and some seems arbitrary (weirdly-chosen associated powers).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before? </div> </div> </div>Very little; just the stuff that winds up in pop culture, and what little bits I got from world history class in high school. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)? </div> </div> </div>I bought several books, actually, and read some scholarly stuff on Vedic gods. I've read the Mahabharata and Ramayana after Scion piqued my interest, and of course there's the countless hours looking up stuff on Wikipedia, for whatever that's worth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1160-luminous-crayon","name":"Luminous Crayon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T11:32:05-08:00","id":12198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't fuck with Vishnu.<br /> <img src=\"http://www.harekrsna.de/artikel/bhishma-wheel.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:56:08-08:00","id":13765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone.<br /> <br /> I somehow convinced my teacher in my college course to let me look at the use of Hinduism in table-top RPGs and video games. He allowed this as long as I could actually talk with players of these games and get their opinion. So I have come here to ask you some simple questions and I would really appreciate it if you could help by answering them.<br /> <br /> The questions:<br /> <br /> 1. What do you think of the representation of the pantheons in Scion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Purely for entertainment purposes. Attempting to draw any deeper meaning from the fictional representations is best avoided. There's plenty of actual scholarly work on all of the pantheons that have to date been included in official Scion materials that there's no real excuse for approaching Scion as sole-source for religious education in polytheistic religion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. What did you know about Hinduism before you played Scion? Where did you learn it before?</div> </div> </div> </div>Growing up one of my friends and his family were practicing Hindus. I asked a lot of (in retrospect perhaps insensitive) questions. Then I visited the south Asian subcontinent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loki Duck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/9295-attention-deva-players-and-other-scion-players-really#post9295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Does the game make you want to learn more about the Hindu Gods (or Hindu myth in general)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in particular, no. Nor, should I add, did the game have anything to do with my eventual accession to Asatru. I was encouraged to try and tried nearly every form of worship I could think of. The Hindu faith, while possessed of some of the most vibrant and interesting (and well-preserved) mythology, is simply not compatible with my opinions on social egalitarianism. It's also a dead end on the theological tree, which makes it less interesting than many other polytheistic belief systems, which either diverge from or converge to traditional sky god-centric worship practices.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}